  "summary": "I cleared all 13 messages in the queue (6 patients) under the refill protocol, RBC-RX-05. Each message is closed with links to what was done, and every patient got a reply. Two refills were not given and are waiting for your review.\n\nNeeds your review (tasks assigned to you):\n- Evelyn Brooks (pt-0029), lisinopril, urgent (task-t0009): not refilled. Her dose went up from 10 to 20 mg on 9/21. On the 10/08 BMP her creatinine was 1.24, up 37.8% from 0.90 before the change. The protocol treats a rise over 30% the same as a potassium of 5.5 or higher. Her potassium was 5.2 and eGFR fell from 79 to 54. She says she ran out on 10/20, so she needs a call soon. Her metformin 1000 mg twice daily was given as a 30-day supply with no refills, and I ordered an HbA1c. Her last one was collected 4/14, which is outside the 6-month window.\n- Lena Park (pt-0028), metformin (task-t0008): not refilled. Her 7/20 kidney results were corrected by the lab: creatinine 1.62 (first reported 1.28), eGFR 39 (first reported 51). Your 7/20 note was based on the first values. I left her current order active rather than holding it. Her lisinopril 10 mg was given as a 30-day supply with no refills. Her last BMP was collected 10/02/2025, more than 12 months ago, so I ordered a new one.\n\nRefilled:\n- Gloria Hayes (pt-0026): lisinopril 20 mg, 90 days with 1 refill. The 10/05 potassium of 6.1 was on a hemolyzed sample, so the protocol doesn't count it. The decision used the 4/14 BMP (potassium 4.6), and I ordered a BMP to repeat the potassium. Her two messages were treated as one request.\n- Frank Odum (pt-0027): lisinopril 10 mg and amlodipine 5 mg, each 90 days with 1 refill. The outside potassium of 5.9 on 8/27 was hemolyzed, so the decision used the 1/20 BMP (potassium 4.5). I ordered a BMP to repeat it.\n- Samuel Price (pt-0030): lisinopril 20 mg, 90 days with 1 refill. On the 10/06 BMP, potassium was 5.2 and creatinine rose 23.6%, under the 30% limit. Metformin 1000 mg twice daily, 90 days with 1 refill: eGFR 65, and an outside HbA1c from 8/19 counts. His two messages and the pharmacy's request for metformin were covered by one order.\n- Marcus Webb (pt-0031): metformin 500 mg twice daily, 90 days with 1 refill. His eGFR was 92 on 9/28; the 10/14 eGFR of 39 was marked entered in error and doesn't count. His HbA1c was 6.9 on 9/28. Lisinopril 10 mg was given as a 30-day supply with no refills, because his last BMP (collected 10/20/2025) is more than 12 months old; I ordered a new one.\n\nEach renewal replaced the patient's old prescription.",
